    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0223" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg107"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/125.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Reinsch.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram May 8th. American Red Cross gratified that Chinese Government is
                    considering proposal of its Minister of Foreign Affairs. If adopted it will
                    probably ensure the results so much desired by that Government and American Red
                    Cross, which organization hopes for speedy and favorable action by Government on
                    said proposal to finance supplemental survey. Meanwhile as further earnest of
                    good faith and unabated interest, the Red Cross will immediately organize and
                    send to China a board of three engineers for verification of Jameson report and
                    estimate. Without such report by eminent engineers it will not be practicable to
                    finance conservancy loan in America. At same time Red Cross will advance needed
                    funds to meet early board expenses, having entire confidence that Government
                    will recognize disinterested motives of Red Cross, and at least share the
                    expenses of further survey for verification.</p>
                <p>Three American engineers highest standing will make this investigation, devoting
                    three months to survey and study, Jameson helping. Meanwhile Red Cross will omit
                    no effort to solve problem of floating the loan, deeming it inopportune to
                    discuss contract for execution until report of engineering board is
                    available.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
